{
 "id": "polyjet-fingertip-mm",
 "kind": "multimat",
 "brief": "A soft fingertip for the parallel jaw on my robot, to be printed on a Stratasys PolyJet in\nVeroWhite and Agilus30 in one build. It screws to the jaw's flat face at y = 0 with two M2.5\nscrews along Y at (x, z) = (-5, 6) and (5, 6), into 2.2 mm pilot holes 8 mm deep from that\nface (y = 0 to 8), with 2 mm of rigid material round each hole. The tip fits in x = -9 to 9,\ny = 0 to 18, z = 0 to 12. The front (+Y) face is what grips: the front 3 mm (y = 15 to 18,\nthe whole face) must be Agilus30 so it conforms to the part, backed by rigid Vero; the screw\narea must be Vero. Loads: it's held by the screws against the jaw; squeeze is 15 N on the\nfront face pushing in -Y, and lift is the squeeze plus 6 N along -Z (the object's weight\ndragging on the pad, which shears the soft-rigid bond). Safety factor 2 on both materials and\non the bond, and keep it under 6 g.",
 "attachments": [],
